#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS: Home Assistant integration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"This page describes the Home Assistant integration **“Fenecon FEMS & "
"OpenEMS”** (ha_openems, version 1.8.0, installation via HACS, at least Home "
"Assistant 2026.8.0). It is a third-party project and **not** part of OpenEMS "
"or FENECON. It is based on the source code of the integration and the "
"OpenEMS source code; it has not been tried out here."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The page xref:user/third-party/overview.adoc[Third-party systems on OpenEMS] "
"gives a comparison with evcc and openWB."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"In short: like the web interface, the integration connects to the system via "
"the xref:user/external-interfaces/websocket.adoc[websocket], turns "
"components into devices and values (“channels”) into entities in Home "
"Assistant, receives the values live and can change **settings**. It only "
"sets **control values** (e.g. “charge the storage with 2 kW now”) via an "
"additional service that uses the xref:user/external-interfaces/rest-"
"control.adoc[REST interface]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setting up the connection"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setting-up-the-connection
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"When adding the integration, you specify the address, user name and "
"password. For a local system, the user name is arbitrary (the instructions "
"mention “x”); what matters is the password, which determines the role (see "
"xref:user/external-interfaces/websocket.adoc#sec-functions-and-user-"
"roles[User roles]). The connection type is selected under “More options”:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Connection type\n"
"| Address\n"
"| Remote station\n"
"\n"
"| Direct connection to the system (default)\n"
"| ws://system:8085/\n"
"| Websocket interface of the Edge (Controller.Api.Websocket)\n"
"| FEMS local\n"
"| ws://system:80/websocket\n"
"| Web interface of the FEMS, which forwards to the websocket\n"
"| OpenEMS local\n"
"| ws://host:8082/\n"
"| your own OpenEMS backend (port 8082 is its default for the interface)\n"
"| FENECON online monitoring\n"
"| wss://portal.fenecon.de/…\n"
"| FENECON backend via the internet\n"
"| Custom address\n"
"| free\n"
"| e.g. behind a proxy\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"For all local types, the connection is **unencrypted** (ws, not wss). "
"Password and data therefore pass through the home network in plain text. "
"Home Assistant stores the credentials in its own configuration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"For a backend with several systems, the integration queries the list of "
"systems (20 at most) and creates one entry per system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "How communication works"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-communication-works
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The integration uses the same commands as the web interface (see xref:user/"
"external-interfaces/websocket.adoc#sec-what-happens-after-opening-the-web-"
"interface[What happens after opening the web interface]). All requests to "
"the system are wrapped in an “edgeRpc” envelope with the system ID. This "
"also works with the direct connection because the Edge also understands this "
"envelope."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "During setup"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-during-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"Open the connection and log in with user name and password. The integration "
"logs in again with the password for each connection; a login token is not "
"used."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-during-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "Read the configuration of the system: which components exist."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-during-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"Query the list of channels (with type, unit, read/write access) for **each** "
"component individually. With 20 to 50 components, this is the same number of "
"requests."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-during-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"Read the host name of the system and the names (aliases) of the components "
"once via a second, short connection. The device names are created from this."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-during-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"Save the result of steps 2 to 4 in the entry of the integration in Home "
"Assistant."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-during-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "Create a device for each component and an entity for each channel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "At every start of Home Assistant"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-at-every-start-of-home-assistant
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "Open the connection and log in as above."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-at-every-start-of-home-assistant
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The components, channels and names are **not** read anew from the system. "
"The integration uses the list saved during setup or the last reload."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-at-every-start-of-home-assistant
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "Create devices and entities from this list; existing ones are reused."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "When reloading"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-when-reloading
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "Steps 2 to 5 of setup run again if"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-when-reloading
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "you “reload” or reconfigure the entry in Home Assistant, or"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-when-reloading
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "the saved list is empty."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-when-reloading
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The same applies if the system could not be reached when Home Assistant "
"started. Home Assistant then only repeats the attempt when it has fully "
"started up. If the connection succeeds, the integration reads the list anew "
"as when reloading."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-when-reloading
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The list is not read anew in the event of a connection failure with "
"reconnection (see below) and when changing the options, i.e. when activating "
"or deactivating components."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "During operation"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-during-operation
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The integration registers the system and the list of **activated** entities "
"(“subscribe”). Only activated entities are subscribed to; all others cost "
"nothing during operation."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-during-operation
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "The system sends the values of these channels about **every second**."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-during-operation
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"If entities are activated or deactivated, the integration adjusts the "
"subscription within about 5 seconds."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-during-operation
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"Optionally (“Limit data updates”), it only passes on the values to Home "
"Assistant every N seconds. This reduces the amount of data in the Home "
"Assistant database; the system still sends every second."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connection failure"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-connection-failure
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"If no values arrive for **60 seconds**, the connection is considered lost."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-connection-failure
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "All entities then become “unavailable”."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-connection-failure
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The integration tries to re-establish the connection every 10 seconds, logs "
"in again and subscribes again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is not transferred"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-is-not-transferred
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"**No history from the system.** The integration does not read any stored "
"histories (see xref:user/data/history-rrd4j.adoc[History]). Home Assistant "
"builds its own history from the live values. If Home Assistant is not "
"running, a gap arises there even though the system continues to record."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-is-not-transferred
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"**Configuration changes in the system** (new component, new app) are not "
"adopted automatically. To do this, you must “reload” the entry in Home "
"Assistant. According to the code, the message from the system about a "
"changed configuration is currently not evaluated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What appears in Home Assistant"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| OpenEMS\n"
"| Home Assistant\n"
"\n"
"| System\n"
"| Entry of the integration (name from the host name)\n"
"| Component (e.g. ess0, meter0, ctrlEvcs0)\n"
"| Device\n"
"| Measured value (e.g. power, state of charge)\n"
"| Sensor\n"
"| Yes/no value (e.g. warnings)\n"
"| Binary sensor\n"
"| Yes/no setting\n"
"| Switch\n"
"| Setting with selection list\n"
"| Select\n"
"| Setting with number\n"
"| Number (only for stored settings, see below)\n"
"| Setting with time\n"
"| Time (only for stored settings)\n"
"| System update of the system\n"
"| Update entity\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"**Default:** After setup, only some components and only a few channels "
"within them are active, including the total values (`+_sum+`: consumption, "
"production, grid, storage), state of charge and energy meter of the storage, "
"power of meters and PV inverters, the emergency reserve, the charge point "
"settings, grid-optimized charge, battery extension, § 14a and the release "
"for charging from the grid. Further components can be added in the options "
"of the integration, further entities activated in the entity list. The "
"instructions advise against activating several hundred channels at the same "
"time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The energy meters from `+_sum+` (grid purchase, feed-in, production, storage "
"charge and discharge, see xref:user/basics/energy-flows.adoc[Energy flows]) "
"are suitable for the Home Assistant **energy dashboard**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additional calculated values"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-additional-calculated-values
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"For batteries, the integration itself calculates the **voltage difference** "
"between the highest and lowest cell, for the entire battery and per module. "
"OpenEMS does not supply these values directly; they are created from the "
"cell voltages (see xref:user/systems/fenecon-home-battery.adoc[FENECON Home "
"battery]). For this, the cell voltage channels must be activated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ready-made cards"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-ready-made-cards
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The integration comes with templates for dashboard cards: charge point, grid-"
"optimized charge, emergency reserve, heating element and a battery "
"diagnostics dashboard. They need additional card extensions from HACS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What can be controlled"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-can-be-controlled
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "The integration has three write routes. They differ fundamentally:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Route\n"
"| What\n"
"| How\n"
"| Duration\n"
"| Required role\n"
"\n"
"| Changing a setting\n"
"| Switch, select, number, time; action “Update component configuration”\n"
"| updateComponentConfig via the websocket\n"
"| **permanent**, is stored\n"
"| Owner\n"
"| Setting a control value\n"
"| Action “REST write sensor” on a sensor\n"
"| POST to the REST interface of the system\n"
"| temporary, only as long as repeated\n"
"| according to the REST page Owner; REST write app required\n"
"| System update\n"
"| Update entity “Install”\n"
"| Call to `+_host+` via the websocket\n"
"| –\n"
"| Owner\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The integration does not use the websocket command for setting control "
"values (setChannelValue); in OpenEMS it is reserved for the Admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-settings
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"Each setting of a component (channels starting with “_Property”) becomes an "
"entity:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-settings
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"**Yes/no settings** always become switches, for **every** component. This "
"also includes “enabled” (`+_PropertyEnabled+`), which can be used to switch "
"off a component completely. These switches are deactivated by default but "
"available."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-settings
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"**Selection lists** are created if the system supplies the options or the "
"integration knows them, e.g. charging mode and priority at the charge point, "
"mode of grid-optimized charge, mode of the heating element, power "
"distribution strategy (`+_power+`), risk level of the energy optimizer."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-settings
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"**Numbers** only for settings for which the integration has stored limits: "
"emergency reserve (percent), energy limit and minimum power values at the "
"charge point, energy limit at the EVSE charge point, minimum running time of "
"the heating element."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-settings
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"**Times**: target time of grid-optimized charge, end time of the heating "
"element."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-settings
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"With the action **“Update component configuration”** "
"(“update_component_config”), several settings of a component can be changed "
"in **one** request. The integration only checks whether a value is a number, "
"a switch value, a time or a valid selection; it does not check the minimum "
"and maximum values of numbers. For charge points (ctrlEvcs), the integration "
"sends both settings together when changing the charging mode and when "
"switching on “Charging enabled”."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-settings
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"**Important – memory wear:** Every change to a setting is **stored "
"permanently** in the system and restarts the function concerned. Automations "
"that switch settings frequently (for example every minute) can wear out the "
"flash memory of the system in the long term. See xref:user/external-"
"interfaces/websocket.adoc#sec-note-do-not-write-the-configuration-"
"frequently[Note: Do not write the configuration frequently]. Therefore only "
"write settings in automations rarely and only when there is a real change."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Control values via REST"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-values-via-rest
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"For ongoing control, e.g. specifying a storage power or switching a relay, "
"there is the action **“REST write sensor”** (or “REST write binary sensor” "
"for binary sensors). It only works if the app or component **“REST/JSON API "
"read/write access”** (Controller.Api.Rest.ReadWrite) is set up in the "
"system; the integration recognizes this during setup."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-values-via-rest
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The integration sends the value via HTTP to `+/rest/channel/component/"
"channel+` of the system, with the same credentials as for the websocket (see "
"xref:user/external-interfaces/rest-control.adoc#sec-setting-a-control-"
"value[Setting a control value])."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-values-via-rest
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"Because the system discards a control value after the Api-Timeout (default "
"60 seconds), the integration **repeats** the value every 30 seconds by "
"default. “Timeout” can be used to specify for how long; 0 means “until the "
"next call for this entity”. “Update cycle 0” only sends once."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-values-via-rest
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"A control value is only held in RAM; this is the right route for frequent "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-values-via-rest
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"You **cannot** see in Home Assistant whether the value has arrived: the "
"system does not report written control values back. Only errors (e.g. wrong "
"password, “is not a Write Channel”) appear in the Home Assistant log."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-control-values-via-rest
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The integration always forms the REST address as an unencrypted address "
"(http) from the host name of the websocket address and the port set in the "
"REST app (default 8084). There is no address you can specify yourself for "
"this. If the system is behind a proxy that only forwards the websocket under "
"this host name and not the REST port, the integration cannot reach the REST "
"app. This route does not exist with FENECON online monitoring."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "System update"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-system-update
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The update entity queries the update status of the system every 12 hours and "
"can start an update. This requires the Owner role and only works where the "
"system itself offers a system update."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Limit\n"
"| Consequence\n"
"\n"
"| Third-party project, not from the manufacturer\n"
"| Changes to OpenEMS or FEMS can affect the integration at any time. According to the instructions, only a FENECON Home 10 with a few additional devices has been tested.\n"
"| Guest role\n"
"| Read only. Switches, selections etc. appear, but changing them fails.\n"
"| Settings are stored permanently\n"
"| Frequent switching wears out the memory of the system; use REST control values for ongoing control.\n"
"| Control values only via REST\n"
"| REST write app required, no feedback in Home Assistant, value must be repeated.\n"
"| Dangerous switches available\n"
"| E.g. “enabled” of each component. Anyone who activates such entities can switch off storage, meters or protective functions.\n"
"| No history from the system\n"
"| Gaps in Home Assistant when it is not running.\n"
"| Configuration is not automatically updated\n"
"| “Reload” after changes to the system.\n"
"| Unencrypted connection in the home network\n"
"| Do not expose port 8085 or 8084 to the internet.\n"
"| Many entities\n"
"| Load and data volume in Home Assistant; subscription only for activated entities.\n"
"| Meter readings after restart of the system\n"
"| According to the code of the integration, the system sometimes reports meter readings that are too low shortly after a restart. The option “Ignore decreasing if total increasing” discards such values so that the statistics in Home Assistant do not jump.\n"
"| Several systems on one backend\n"
"| At most 20 are listed.\n"
"| System limits continue to apply\n"
"| Emergency reserve, battery and grid limits restrict specifications; a control value is not always implemented in full.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "**Can I have the storage charged or discharged from Home Assistant?**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"Yes, via the action “REST write sensor” on the entity for the setpoint power "
"of the storage, e.g. `+ess0/SetActivePowerEquals+` (negative = charge). The "
"prerequisite is the REST write app. The entity must be activated in Home "
"Assistant for this. The integration repeats the value until the timeout "
"expires or a new call arrives."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"**Why does nothing change in Home Assistant after I have written a REST "
"value?**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The control value itself is not reported back. Only the effect can be seen, "
"e.g. in the actual storage power."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"**I set up a new app in the system, but it is missing in Home Assistant.**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"Reload the entry of the integration and add the new component in the options."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"**The system log says “Unable to read value for Channel [meter1/"
"ActivePower]” every second even though the meter is deactivated.**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The message does not come from the meter, but from the websocket interface: "
"Home Assistant queries values of a component that is deactivated in the "
"system. The integration also offers deactivated components, but the system "
"does not supply any values for them and writes this warning in every cycle. "
"Remedy: deselect the component in the options of the integration or "
"deactivate its entities in Home Assistant. If the component is no longer "
"needed in the system at all, you can also delete it there."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "**May I adjust the emergency reserve daily via automation?**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"Occasionally yes. Each change is stored permanently; several times a day is "
"still not critical, every minute is (see xref:user/external-interfaces/"
"websocket.adoc#sec-note-do-not-write-the-configuration-frequently[Note])."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid "**Websocket or REST for Home Assistant?**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-typical-questions
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
msgid ""
"The integration uses both: the websocket for live values and settings, REST "
"only for control values. For a comparison, see xref:user/external-interfaces/"
"websocket.adoc#sec-websocket-or-rest[Websocket or REST?]."
msgstr ""
